A||N||14||Seanh||Car was broken into tonight! ||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||11-26-2001||10:56 PM||||Hey guys, I know I'v read thru some stories from you about people who have had things stolen from your vehicals...Well, tonight I stay late at the store and had my car parked in the parking lot, (pretty remote, no other cars in view), and I was in the office working on the computer. I heard a car outside,  reved it's engine a couple times and I have a buddy who's car sounds like that, so I took off and looked outside, but saw nothing once I got there, only a car going around a far corner out of sight...About an hour later after I'm done I walk out to my car to start it up and the door's unlocked, I thought it odd since I was pretty sure it was looked when I went in, but I left once in between and I may have forgottten to lock then...Next I see snow in the car, from shoes, and I thought it odd to, and next my trim ring for the stereo is on the floor and the stereo is gone and the dash torn up to get it out. I called the cops and they made the report and all, but I'm really wondering if anythings going to happen? Do they usally ever catch these guys? If so how often? Is it very likely I'll ever get my stereo back, or money for it? Sorry but I'm just very upset right now and would really like to know...Thanks for any info and past results!<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly - 86 GT<BR>Back to my 3.1L...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||CoolBlue87GT||11-26-2001||11:06 PM||||Aw man, that sucks. Wish you luck.<P>I had a radio stolen once, the insurance company paid, and I replaced it with a better one.<P>Luckly, mine was a 'pull out' style radio, and didn't have any damage.<P>Gook luck.||||reg||6
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||11-26-2001||11:08 PM||||my SE was stolen very shortly after I bought it.. I even went and found the place where it had been taken to.. was sitting in the driveway.. but it was gone shortly afterwards, no sign of it since.<P>I hope you have better luck with your stereo..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||kempo||11-26-2001||11:10 PM||||This really sucks, I have no respect for thievs, I hope they get caught.  My sisters Saturn was broken into and her basic, cheap, bottom of the line CD Player was stolen, the bastards broke the entire dash to get at it, for what, a $120 headunit?  Anyway, her Saturn is fully insured and they picked up every penny worth of damage as well as the theft items, the cd player and cds and all, minus the deductible.  Her car is fully insured, or else they wouldn't have paid a dime.  Car alarms are pretty useless nowdays as it is.  After she filed the report, the police took some broken dash pieces as evidence, but usually there is no way to catch the thief.  If they do catch the theif, you will probably not see your equipment again, as they steal your stuff and sell it to make a quick $20.  Damn it really pisses me off.  I really hope you find the guy, if for no other reason, to beat the unholy hell out of em!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pyric||11-26-2001||11:27 PM||||Man, that bites.  Sad thing is they probably caused more damage to your dash than the stereo was worth.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>The stereo I'm looking at has a built in alarm system that Blasts your stereo when they touch it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>(Of course then they'd probably wet my front seat)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||11-26-2001||11:31 PM||||I'm looking for that security system that slowly and quietly lowers a chome 44 mag out of the ceiling and shoots them in the head, I'd gladly be willing to clean up the body and blood from my car everytime someone breaks into it...||||reg||1
Z||000006||G-Nasty||11-27-2001||01:39 AM||||I went out one morning and found my decklid was open. I thought I left it open-but nope.<BR>They broke passenger window and stole my Cd player. They didnt tear up interior or even scratch console. Pretty weird - I guess they had good tools. $500 later I replaced cd player with DEH P47-DH (best player for fiero) and got a New window w/ tint-I didnt file a police report because I dont have comprehensive insurance and I currently have 2 warrants. They caught 2 teens for breaking into a bunch of cars in the area.   ||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||11-27-2001||04:17 AM||||I keep coming back to the little 'surprise' that John Travolta had in his TVR's trunk in the movie 'swordfish'.....<P>Thieves get no sympathy, they can be evolved out of the gene pool as far as I am concerned.<P>PS: isn't spending an hour breaking into someone's car, maybe cutting your fingers, then looking quietly for a few more hours for a place to hawk the radio...  rather a *HARD* twenty bucks to earn?!<P>These fricking theves aren't even smart, they'd be better off in just time and money working at a blinking McDonalds!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||Reality||11-27-2001||07:34 AM||||just to give the an idea of teh intellence of the idoits here. I've had my broken into two times both times yuo can tell they were trying to get the radio out but both times they obivously decided it wasn't worth the effort. First time they brokes the trim plate second time they didn't do any damage. Just thought I would share.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/realitysignature_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pheagey||11-27-2001||08:59 AM||||   Seanh, I feel your pain. My car was broken into 'bout a month back &lt;f*cking fa*et as* bast*rds&gt;. As for the cops gettin' the ppl: probley not. Hope you have full insurance.<BR>   Atleast they didn;t steal your tires w/ your own jack....<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed;<BR>Have you seen my website yet?<BR>Http://www.LithiumEffects/pheageysfeiro<BR>"The car formaly know as, and has now reverted back to being known as, Pheagey's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000010||Hybrid2M6||11-27-2001||11:58 AM||||Well, count me into the "broken into club". I was woke up buy my neighbors wife at about 8:00 this mornig to find out that three cars in my apartments lot got broke into last nite. They got three cars in a row. My neighbors, mygirlfriend, an then mine, last. You could tell thats exactly what order they did it too. Mine was the only one with an alarm. They broke the passenger window as it was in the shadows. Left the door locked and leaned over the glass and checked behind the drivers seat only, as the alarm was going off. My cdplayer wasnt touched, even though the faceplate was behind the seat that they stole a speaker out from behind. Why would you not steal the cd player if you found the face to it behind the seat? So how much am I looking at for a new window? I found on going for $20 on ebay, should I bid?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/customgfx.jpg"> <BR>1986 SE IronDuke<BR>Adjustable Touring Wing<BR>American Racing Carrera's<BR> -225/50VR16 Falken Ziex 502<BR> -225/45ZR17 Falken Azenis<BR>Cleared and Painted(red) Tail lights||||reg||8
Z||000011||4UMLA1||11-27-2001||12:44 PM||||I guess I am lucky compared to you guys.  The first thing that I did after I got my car was to have an alarm installed in it, it's a Viper Alarm.  The sensitivity is set so high that even if a truck goes by my car when the alarm is on it will go off.  Most of the people where I live at know how I am about my car, so they don't get near it anyway, but if they do I can always depend on the Viper to send them on there way real quick like.<BR>Sorry to hear about your car, hope they catch those bastards that did it, but I really wouldn't count on it to much <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
